 "about_text": "Charlie James Gallery opened in 2008 in Los Angeles' Chinatown and has built a program centered on emerging and established artists with distinct, often political voices. The gallery works across painting, sculpture, textile, installation, and new media, with particular attention to marginalized perspectives and narratives touching on identity, race, gender, and broader socio-political concerns. Under gallery director Ever Velasquez, the program has become known for thoughtful, provocative curatorial approaches, including annual group exhibitions, and for close collaboration with museums and academics to help place artists' work within broader critical and historical conversations. The gallery now operates two adjoining spaces on historic Chung King Road.",
